package cli

var usage = "soho — role-agent layer over the `herdr` CLI.\n\nRoles are markdown files with frontmatter (roles/<role>.md, overridable per\nproject in .agents/herdr-roles/<role>.md). The native command spawns one CLI agent\nper role in a Herdr pane, dispatches a composed prompt (role body + brief),\nand detects completion through a file-based report contract. Only the `job` supervisor pushes the job branch and opens a draft pull request;\nnothing else commits or pushes, and nothing closes panes it did not\ncreate.\n\nUsage:\n  soho init                          # doctor + name the caller `orchestrator`, print context\n  soho title \"<objective>\" | title --clear   # this pane's title: orchestrator: <objective>\n  soho doctor [--fix] [--panes 2|3|4] [--user|--session]\n                                             # advisory check; --fix normalizes lanes in the project file\n  soho explain                       # plain text for a person: what is running, or how to start\n  soho setup [--local | --target FILE] [--no-hooks] [--dry-run]\n                     [--detect | --probe [--kind K --model M] [--timeout S]\n                      | --plan [--panes 2|3|4] [--lane name=kind[:model[:effort]]]\n                        [--set K V] [--user-set K V] [--session-set K V]]\n                     [--panes 2|3|4] [--lane name=kind[:model[:effort]]]\n                                             # write the block + hooks; --local uses CLAUDE.local.md and Git info/exclude; --detect/--probe/--plan print and write nothing\n  soho hook reminder|doctor          # native advisory agent hooks, silent outside Herdr\n  soho install [--version vTAG] [--dir PATH]\n                                             # portable installer: downloads the release binary for this platform, verifies it against SHA256SUMS, installs it to --dir (default $SOHO_INSTALL_DIR, or $HOME/.local/bin on POSIX / %LOCALAPPDATA%/Programs/soho on Windows); prints the installed path, digest and PATH advice (no automatic shell or registry edits)\n  soho roles [--json] | kinds\n  soho config [set <key> <value> [--project|--user]]\n  soho session [set <key> <value> | clear [key] | show]\n                                             # this-session overrides in <state>/session.conf\n  soho models <kind>                 # ids the CLI lists, newest first\n  soho model <kind> <spec> [effort]  # how a model spec resolves\n  soho regrid                        # exact grids: caller tab (layout=split) + every herd tab\n  soho promote                       # promote this calling sub-orchestrator to orchestrator\n                                             # keeps its pane; refuses unresolved tasks, active collaborations and owned live resources\n  soho tab-label [<text>] [--tab ID] [--auto]\n                                             # list herd tabs / pin a tab's label / back to automatic\n  soho layout-plan [--layout FILE] [--me P] [--mine \"P…\"]\n                                             # where the next split-layout spawn would go, and why\n  soho role <name>\n  soho spawn <role> [--name N] [--kind K] [--direction right|down]\n                      [--ratio F] [--cwd DIR] [--pane ID] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--effort low|medium|high|xhigh|max] [--model M]\n                      [--approvals ask|edits|full] [--mcp inherit|none] [--reuse|--fresh]\n                      [--tab-label TEXT] [--force] [-- <native agent args>]\n  soho env                          # environment block for a feedback issue\n  soho lint <brief.md> [--role <role>]  # check the dispatch brief diagnostics without dispatching\n  soho send <ref|name> <message…> | --file <path> [--now] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--assignment ID --type review.question]\n                                             # peer message to an agent of any kind (a reference, or a name on the local server); waits for a busy target to settle by default; the target project's inbound=off refuses (exit 18)\n  soho dispatch <agent> <brief.md> [--role R] [--timeout MS]\n                      [--no-wait] [--allow-same-family] [--amend] [--for <author>[,…]]\n                      [--compact] [--resend] [--queue]\n                                             # --amend sends <file> as an amendment to the agent's current brief, with a new report that wait watches\n                                             # --compact compacts an idle worker (claude, codex, pi) before the brief; a timeout or a busy worker exits 9/10 and the brief is not sent\n                                             # --resend sends the brief again when the same brief of the task is already open; the default sends nothing and waits on the task's current report (duplicate_of in the JSON)\n                                             # --queue types the brief now to a worker that is still working or blocked on its open task (today's queued behavior); without it the dispatch refuses (exit 10) until the report exists\n  soho compact <agent> [--timeout MS]\n                                             # send /compact once to an idle worker and wait for the CLI's proof plus its return to idle; a kind without a verified command exits 2, a timeout 9 (status timeout JSON)\n  soho wait <agent>... [--timeout MS] [--any]\n  soho status [<agent>...]           # no names = the whole team; gone = agent_not_found; not-in-roster = known to Herdr, not this workspace's team; unavailable = agent get failed (exit 4)\n  soho collect <agent> [--lines N] [--verify]\n                                             # --verify checks the sha256 lines of the last report (exit 16 on changed/missing, or when no sha256 line is found)\n  soho stats [--since <date>] [--by role|kind|model|agent|effort] [--json]  # tasks, times and review findings; --by groups results\n  soho metrics mark <report> [--finding <n>=real|false]... [--missed P0|P1|P2|P3]... [--amendment implementer|brief]\n                                             # label a report after checking it (its metrics line was recorded with metrics=on)\n  soho metrics export [--since <date>] [--project-label <label>]\n                                             # anonymized summary of metrics.jsonl, one JSON line per report\n  soho metrics table [--write <file>] <export.jsonl>...\n                                             # markdown table per role, slice type and model from exported summaries; --write replaces the generated block of <file>\n  soho run <role> <brief.md> [spawn/dispatch options] [-- <agent args>]\n  soho collaborate start <author> <reviewer> --brief <path> [--max-rounds N]\n                      | status <assignment> [--json]\n                      | event <assignment> ready|findings|corrected|approved|escalate --report <path> --revision <fingerprint>\n                      | stop <assignment>\n                      | finalize <assignment> --verdict accept|reject\n                                             # optional worker_messages=policy; assigned local pair; orchestrator creates/finalizes; typed events bind the reviewed revision\n  soho job start --id <id> --repo <org/repo> [--base <branch>] [--mode worktree|workspace]\n                       [--brief <file|->] [--timeout <minutes>] [--dry-run]\n  soho job status --id <id>\n  soho job wait --id <id> [--timeout MS]\n  soho job events --id <id> [--since <seq>] [--wait MS]\n  soho job collect --id <id> [--md] [--verify]\n  soho job amend --id <id> [<file>|-]\n  soho job send --id <id> [<file>|-]\n  soho job ack --id <id> --upto <seq>\n  soho job cancel --id <id> [--grace <seconds>]\n  soho job close --id <id> [--force]\n  soho job list [--state <state>]\n  soho job supervise --id <id> [--repo <org/repo>]\n  soho job checkpoint --id <id>\n  soho job note --id <id> --tipo <type> [--escopo global|projeto] [--motivo <text>] [--refs k=v,...] [<summary>|-]\n  soho capabilities --json            # shared engine capability schema\n  soho roster [--scope workspace|server] [--json]\n  soho find [words] [--machine <label>]... [--all] [--json] [--timeout MS]\n                                             # live panes with a paste-ready session reference ([machine/]<pane id>)\n  soho release <agent> [--close] [--force] [--keep-copies] [--keep-procs]\n                                             # --keep-copies leaves the agent's registered copies for gc instead of removing them\n                                             # --keep-procs leaves the agent's registered processes for gc instead of stopping them\n  soho reopen <agent> [--force]\n                                             # release --close + spawn --fresh with the roster's role, kind, model, effort, cwd and native args (output: the spawn JSON)\n  soho clean [--older-than DAYS]\n  soho copies\n                                             # list the copy registry: <path>  <owner>  <age>  <state> (owned | orphan | missing); read-only\n  soho copies add <path> [--agent <name>]\n                                             # register a copy made by hand (origin add); a path that fails the safety check or is not an existing directory refuses (exit 2), an unknown --agent exits 3\n  soho procs\n                                             # list the process registry: <pid>  <name>  <owner>  <age>  <state> (running | gone | reused); read-only\n  soho procs add <pid> [--agent <name>]\n                                             # register a worker process (its start time and command name; the command line is never read); a pid that is not a positive integer, pid 1, this process, its parent, or not running refuses (exit 2), an unknown --agent exits 3\n  soho gc [--yes] [--older-than HOURS] [--include-unregistered]\n                                             # dry run lists orphan copies at least HOURS old (default 2) plus unregistered mutation copies; --yes removes them (unregistered only with --include-unregistered)\n  soho friction [--since D] [--level L] [--command C] [--agent A] [--summary]  # errors/warnings of this workspace; options AND together\n  soho friction add \"<text>\" [--brief <path>]  # record one friction note (level note, command friction)\n  soho feedback send <report.md> \"<one-line summary>\"\n                                             # feedback=local: file the report in feedback_dir; one line to feedback_to when set\n  soho mutation-guard <copy-dir> [--source <dir>] [--env NAME]...\n  soho mutation-copy [--source <dir>] [--dest <dir>] [--link <relpath>=<target>]...\n\nDurations: --timeout (and job events --wait) takes milliseconds, or a number with ms, s, m or h (90s, 30m, 2h).\n\nCompletion contract: without an assignment, a worker finishes when its report exists.\nAn active collaboration has phase/round/revision/delivery; only orchestrator finalize\nends it. Reports remain round evidence, and release refuses active participants. Use\n`dispatch` (waits by default), `wait` (one or many agents), or `status`\n(non-blocking). Never poll `herdr agent get` state alone: integrations\nreport idle/done mid-task.\n\nConfiguration (key=value files; later layers win, env wins over files,\nflags win over env):\n  <skill>/config.defaults → ~/.config/soho/config\n  → <repo>/.agents/soho.conf → <state>/session.conf (session)\n  → SOHO_<KEY> → flags\n\nExit codes: 2 usage/env · 3 unknown role/agent · 4 Herdr failure (includes\n`herdr agent get` transport/permission errors reported as `unavailable`) ·\n5 same-family reviewer · 6 settled without report or agent really gone ·\n7 agent blocked (startup or approval) or asked a question · 8 max_workers reached ·\n9 wait timeout · 10 lane busy · 11 quota exhausted · 12 planner is the orchestrator ·\n13 lane kind-mismatch (set lane.<name>.kind, or release the lane) ·\n14 provider error or capacity · 15 prompt not received, or send not\ntaken (lost / unverified) ·\n16 collect --verify: a reported file changed or is missing, or nothing was verified ·\n17 send: the target is still busy after the wait timeout, or shows a\ndialog; nothing was sent ·\n18 send: the target project refuses peer messages (inbound=off) ·\n19 job failed · 20 job id reused with another brief · 21 job canceled ·\n22 job preparation failed · 24 job close with unacknowledged decisions ·\n25 spawn refused under resource pressure.\n"
